# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2/C2-3): catalogued in the #ext kpkg block, never
# as an ordinary entry; installs /stand/k30/{unix,kabi,unix.sym} and the
# cut's ufs and s5 modules at /etc/conf/mod.d (C2-3 v8 sec 1).  The module
# kernel (family generic, kabi k30.1.3), build id 68030-261031-64 (uname -m,
# kinfo); its own package, not a revision of kernel-k30-u (C2-3 sec 1.1).
APKG_DESC=The 68030 module kernel (kabi k30.1.3, loader 2): /stand/k30/unix (brel) + kabi + unix.sym, with no built-in ufs or s5: it carries the ufs and s5 modules built with it (/etc/conf/mod.d); drivers such as z3660eth come as module packages; kbootset composes them into a boot generation.  Upgrade together with kbootset -22 or later.  New in kabi 1.3: /dev/paula support (the paula-k30 module package), and a /dev/audio open that fails at once (EIO) when Paula never interrupts instead of hanging the box.  New in -56: shrinking a big file (ftruncate, tar --delete, dd seek=) no longer panics the kernel; a file shrunk and then regrown sparsely no longer reads its old bytes back; a 68030 without an FPU no longer panics at the first signal.  New in -63: a STREAMS queue still scheduled is no longer freed under the scheduler, so a unix-socket server under client traffic (prngd with prngd-ctl) no longer panics the kernel.  New in -64: the kernel knows the random module's major (c 48), so the random module package (/dev/random, /dev/urandom) loads.
DESC=The module kernel of the 030 line (the loadable-modules plan; S5-10, the k30 kernel with ufs and s5 carved out): the K030-U recipe with kinfo and the amix-dlm module core (the module core of amix kernel/dlm b391504: the four-card sd layer, the halt hook, the sd seam, bdevsw row 20 freed, the root pass: root-class modules loaded from the arena, dlm_marc_root, root_defer, iodone, ramdisk_image and vfs_register; the arena 16-aligned; the five DDI 1.2 DMA names with the core's 030 DMA provider; the 13 filesystem names and the 100 core-tier names the filesystem modules bind to; the safe boot modules; DDI minor 3, kabi k30.1.3: AllocMem, FreeMem, displaytype, paula_busy and audio_nopen for the paula module, the kernel listing only the names of its own minor; the major registry with c 48 random) linked in, with the stock audio driver patched by amix-paula 1b2736d (MIT: while /dev/paula is open /dev/audio refuses its open and the other way round; a safe close after a killed player; the open's wait for Paula's first interrupt is bounded, so a silent Paula fails the open with EIO instead of spinning), with the 040/060 port's rth1 at 0d37eb1 (AXL1's RAM-disk root selector and rootfstype, swap /dev/fakeswap on a RAM-disk root; a motherboard controller's root record matched by its kinfo id, rth1=2), cut by the k30 station from amix b391504 (kernel/k30/cuts/68030-261031-64), with the STREAMS freeq guard (qdetach, strclose and stropen free a queue through freeq_guarded), shipped in the brel form the amix boot loader binds.  No static A4091/A4092/A4770, Gayle IDE or cdfs: they come as module packages (a4091-k30, gayle-k30, cdfs-k30); the kernel drives the A3000 SCSI and the A2090/A2091 itself (root= mobo:a3000-wd,zorro:0202:01,zorro:0202:03).  Build -64 has no built-in ufs or s5 filesystem: the package carries the ufs and s5 modules as core-tier modules built with this cut (/etc/conf/mod.d/ufs and s5, comment-only /etc/conf/modreg.d files), and the sidecar names no rootfs=; kbootset promotes the root filesystem's module to a root record.  /stand/k30/kabi is the kernel build's sidecar for the brel (kabi=k30.1.3, family=generic, loader-min=2, bss, arena, ident, ksym, abi=, sdcards=, rth1=2, sym=), copied verbatim; /stand/k30/unix.sym holds the brel's symbols for kbootset's namelist.  Upgrade it together with kbootset -22 or later (amix-dlm 1308c0b: a motherboard root record by its kinfo id for an rth1=2 kernel, S5-46, and the core-tier module's tier= and build= in the root record).  The package writes no boot store itself; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).
